# Dependencies
node_modules/
.npm
*.tgz

# Build output
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Environment.
#
# `bloom create` generates real secrets into .env — BLOOM_AUTH_SECRET signs
# every JWT this app issues, and BLOOM_FRONTEND_KEY gates the API. Committing
# it publishes both. Keep .env local and put deployment values in whatever your
# host uses for them.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Local database
*.db
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
prisma/dev.db*

# Logs and runtime
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
*.pid
*.pid.lock
coverage/
.nyc_output/
.eslintcache

# OS and editor
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# ── Two things this deliberately does NOT ignore ──────────────────────────
#
# public/            holds the favicon and the self-hosted fonts. Several
#                    widely-copied Node gitignores carry a bare `public` line
#                    inherited from Gatsby, where it is build output. Here it is
#                    source, and ignoring it drops the fonts — with no error,
#                    just a page that quietly falls back to the system stack.
#
# prisma/migrations/ is schema history, not generated noise. Ignoring it leaves
#                    a fresh clone able to read the schema but unable to rebuild
#                    the database that matches it.
#
# src/web/shared/api-routes.ts is generated by scripts/gen-api-routes.mjs, but
#                    it is regenerated on install, dev, build and typecheck, and
#                    committing it keeps a fresh clone typechecking immediately.
